Verify that in cgroup v2, memory charges remain pinned to the cgroup
that allocated them when a task migrates, and that new allocations after
migration are charged to the destination cgroup.

Signed-off-by: Pavithra <pavrampu@linux.ibm.com>
---
v3 -> v4:
- disable swap on group_a and group_b to prevent false failures from
  memory.current drops under pressure
Link to v3: https://lore.kernel.org/ltp/20260813162337.3012813-1-pavrampu@linux.ibm.com/
